# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: envmap_quad
# The third Stock Effect in the corpus: EnvironmentMapEffect (non-fresnel/non-specular bucket --
# specularEnabled is always false on this renderer, D9-82e's own structurally-unreachable finding,
# so this never sets environmentmapspecular). Reuses the existing PositionNormalTexture vertex
# shape (VSInputNmTx, matches the existing stride-32 layout exactly, D9-82e's own "no new vertex
# declaration needed" finding).
#
# Real formula (D9-82e's own DirectX9_DrawEx check, verified live): result = lerp(texture*diffuseSum,
# environmentMap, environmentMapAmount). A 1x1 white base texture and a 1x1 environment (cube) map
# -- every face deliberately the SAME color, sidestepping any need to hand-compute reflect()
# geometry, the same trick D9-82e's own CTest already used -- lit by one dim directional light
# (diffuse=0.5, matching lit_textured_quad.scene's own convention) and blended half-and-half with
# the environment map (environmentmapamount=0.5).
#
# fresnelfactor=0 IS REQUIRED here, not merely omittable: real XNA's EnvironmentMapEffect
# constructor defaults FresnelFactor to 1 (fresnel ENABLED), confirmed in FNA's own
# EnvironmentMapEffect.cs (`FresnelFactor = 1;` in the constructor) and matched by CNA's own
# EnvironmentMapEffect.cpp constructor. A first version of this scene never set fresnelfactor at
# all, meaning it was ACTUALLY exercising the fresnel-enabled shader bucket the whole time despite
# this file's own comment claiming otherwise -- an undetected documentation error, not a rendering
# bug, that happened not to affect the pixel result only because this scene's own geometry is
# coincidentally degenerate for Fresnel: the quad sits in the SAME z=0 plane as EyePosition=(0,0,0)
# (View is Identity everywhere in this corpus, so EyePosition = Invert(View).Translation = origin),
# so eyeVector always has a zero Z component; with normal=(0,0,1), viewAngle=dot(eyeVector,normal)
# is exactly 0 at every vertex, and pow(max(1-abs(0),0), FresnelFactor) = pow(1, anything) = 1
# regardless of the exponent -- Fresnel-enabled and Fresnel-disabled produce the IDENTICAL blend
# factor (EnvironmentMapAmount) for this specific geometry. Explicitly setting fresnelfactor=0 now
# makes this scene's own "non-fresnel bucket" claim genuinely true rather than accidentally true.
# See envmap_fresnel_quad.scene for a scene that actually exercises Fresnel's view-angle-dependent
# math with a real, non-degenerate per-vertex gradient.
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
effect=EnvironmentMapEffect
vertexformat=PositionNormalTexture
lighting=true
ambientcolor=0,0,0
light0enabled=true
light0diffuse=0.5,0.5,0.5
light0direction=0,0,-1
texture=true
texturewidth=1
textureheight=1
texturefilter=Point
environmentmap=true
environmentmapsize=1
environmentmapamount=0.5
fresnelfactor=0
primitive=TriangleList
texturepixel=255,255,255,255
environmentmappixel=200,100,50,255
# x,y,z,nx,ny,nz,u,v -- every vertex faces the camera (+Z normal), matching lit_textured_quad.scene.
vertex=-0.6,0.6,0,0,0,1,0,0
vertex=0.6,0.6,0,0,0,1,1,0
vertex=-0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,1,0,1
vertex=0.6,0.6,0,0,0,1,1,0
vertex=0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,1,1,1
vertex=-0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,1,0,1
